"- Object 1 Hazelnut\n    - Attribute 1 Type - A single, whole hazelnut with a smooth, rounded shell and a distinct, textured crown at one end.\n    - Attribute 2 Color - The shell displays a gradient of warm brown tones, transitioning from a darker, rough-textured crown to a lighter, glossy brown on the curved body.\n    - Attribute 3 Size - The hazelnut is roughly spherical, with a length and width of approximately 2 to 2.5 centimeters, typical for a mature hazelnut.\n    - Attribute 4 Material - The material is a hard, woody shell, naturally occurring and unprocessed, with a slightly matte finish on the crown and a subtle sheen on the body.\n    - Attribute 5 Composition - The hazelnut shell is composed of a dense, fibrous outer layer (crown) and a smooth, tightly sealed inner shell, both formed from lignified plant tissue.\n    - Attribute 6 Quantity - One hazelnut is present.\n    - Attribute 7 Relative Location - The hazelnut is centered in the frame, occupying the middle of the visual field.\n    - Attribute 8 Orientation - The hazelnut is positioned with its crown facing upward and slightly tilted, revealing the textured top and the smooth, curved side.\n    - Attribute 9 Connection or Attachments - The hazelnut is a standalone object with no visible attachments, connections, or appendages; it is intact and unaltered."